session:pr673Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #466 (part of the code-quality epic #453) asked to bundle the (datastore, active_graph, deadline) triple threaded through the SPARQL executor into an EvalCtx struct, to retire the #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)] sites in sparql_parser's execute module. Before writing EvalCtx, I verified the issue's claim of '7 functions' empirically rather than trusting the description: grepping found only 3 literal #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)] annotations, all in paths.rs. Temporarily removing all 3 and running cargo clippy confirmed exactly 3 warnings at the crate's default 7-argument threshold — so the issue's '7 functions' was a looser count of every function sharing the (datastore, active_graph, deadline) triple, not literally 7 lint sites. Counting parameters across every function in sparql_parser/src/execute/*.rs turned up exactly 7 functions carrying that triple as separate parameters: eval_bgp, eval_triple_pattern, eval_triple_pattern_core (bgp.rs) and eval_path_pattern, eval_repeat_path, eval_exact_repeat, transitive_closure (paths.rs) — matching the issue's count exactly once the right criterion (shares the triple) was used instead of the wrong one (trips the lint today). Designed EvalCtx<'a> as a Copy struct of three borrowed references (datastore, active_graph, deadline), added in execute/mod.rs alongside the pre-existing ActiveGraph enum (widened from private to pub(crate) since EvalCtx now exposes it across submodules). Kept the per-call row `budget: Option<usize>` parameter separate from EvalCtx rather than folding it in, since budget varies per call site (issue #165's row short-circuiting) while EvalCtx's three fields are genuinely contextual and constant for the duration of one evaluation. Added EvalCtx::with_active_graph for the one place (transitive_closure's both-endpoints-unbound branch) that must evaluate a sub-scope against a graph other than the caller's, when iterating every named graph for an unbound GRAPH ?g — relying on EvalCtx's borrowed-reference fields being covariant so a shorter-lived local ActiveGraph can be substituted without a lifetime conflict. All 7 functions' call sites are internal to sparql_parser::execute (verified by grep before starting), so no other crate's code needed touching; eval_component/eval_components_budgeted (components.rs) construct an EvalCtx locally to call the converted functions but keep their own (datastore, active_graph, budget, deadline) signature unchanged, since they weren't part of the issue's flagged set and converting them wasn't needed to retire the allows. Hit a pre-existing, unrelated build break in dagalog-kernel/src/sockets.rs (missing .map_err(CellError::Execution) on the CellType::Functional dispatch arm, already fixed on not-yet-merged PR #663/#662) and applied the same one-line fix locally so the workspace would build; documented as out-of-scope in the PR body per the task brief. Also hit the shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR filling the disk to 100% mid-quality-check (a known hazard per CLAUDE.md, exacerbated by several other worktrees building concurrently) — ran cargo clean to recover 75.8GiB before finishing cargo check/clippy/test. Full cargo test --workspace passed except the documented flaky slow_transitive_closure_query_times_out_with_503 OOM-kill on this memory-constrained dev box (a known false alarm per PR #635's provenance summary and this issue's own task brief), confirmed via CI which ran it green." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:673 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr673 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr673Summary agp:decisionPoint session:pr673Decision .

session:pr673Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Converted exactly the 7 functions that structurally carry (datastore, active_graph, deadline) as separate parameters (eval_bgp, eval_triple_pattern, eval_triple_pattern_core, eval_path_pattern, eval_repeat_path, eval_exact_repeat, transitive_closure) to take a single EvalCtx<'a>, keeping the per-call `budget` parameter separate and leaving eval_component/eval_components_budgeted's own signatures untouched (they build an EvalCtx locally instead)." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered folding eval_component/eval_components_budgeted (and possibly eval_components/eval_independent_then_join) into the EvalCtx refactor too, since they carry the same triple and eval_component's own budget+triple combination is structurally identical to eval_bgp's. Rejected as unnecessary scope growth: none of them trip the too_many_arguments lint today (6 params each, under the 7-arg default threshold), they were not in the issue's enumerated set, and converting them adds churn to call sites in mod.rs without retiring any additional #[allow] — the issue's stated goal (retire the too_many_arguments allows) is fully met by converting only the 7 functions that actually needed it." .
